
Firmware fault snapshot regression tests

Run from the repository root:

    python -m unittest discover -s test -p test_firmware_faults.py -v

The runner compiles the production src/canPowertrain.cpp with lightweight
host fakes for CAN, Arduino timing, EEPROM, and hardware-only headers.
It uses the real include/IOManagement.h and firmware configuration.
Requires Python and a C++17 g++ or clang++ compiler. Set CXX to the compiler
executable path if it is not on PATH. Build artifacts use a temporary directory.
No MCU, CAN adapter, PlatformIO installation, or Python packages are required.

Coverage includes the CAN 0x505 eight-byte wire contract, exact raw BPS
codes, engineering values, startup grace and inclusive limits, misordered
high/low fields, current codes on both sides of 0x8000, transient faults
that recover before transmission, immutable first-fault snapshots,
EEPROM restart behavior, emergency stop, and malformed input frames.
